description: Verification expectations before work is considered complete
alwaysApply: true
---

# Quality Gates

- Treat tests, linting, type checks, builds, and security checks as part of the change, not optional cleanup.
- Run the smallest useful verification first, then broader checks when shared behavior, user flows, or infrastructure are affected.
- Add or update automated tests for bug fixes, user-facing behavior, data transformations, permission checks, and shared utilities.
- Keep verification commands runnable inside the Cursor shell environment and document new commands when they are introduced.
- Tag deploy CI uses `scripts/ci-test.sh` and `scripts/ci-django-check.sh` for verbose, paste-friendly failure logs; prefer those when reproducing a failed Actions run.
- Do not claim verification passed unless it was actually run. If a check cannot run, explain why and name the remaining risk.
- Prefer deterministic checks and fixtures over manual-only validation for behavior future agents may change.
